          "code": "OBJECTIVE",
          "id": "1778459990470",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1778459990470_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Generate a markdown bullet points based on {{$context.$nodes.GET_TACTIC_DETAILS?.$output?.objective}} for {{$context.$nodes.REFINE_PROGRAM_DATA?.$output?.result.ProgramType}} Sales Motion and target product {{$context.$nodes.REFINE_PROGRAM_DATA?.$output?.result.TargetProductName}} \nto drive higher conversion thru pipeline\n\nAlso show messageListWidget in bottom based on Success Criteria from below object. if successCriteria not present show \"No success criteria found\"\n{{$context.$nodes.GET_SUCCESS_CRITERIA.$output.result}}\n\n<oraInfoDisplay key=\"system-alerts\">\n{\n  \"patternId\": \"messageListWidget\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"subtitle\": \"Real-time metrics\",\n    \"items\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": <title>,\n        \"summary\": <summary>,\n        \"priority\": \"neutral\",\n        \"image\": use \"data:image/png;base64,\"\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n</oraInfoDisplay>\n\nconsider below for title and summary value\n\nGuidelines:\n\ntitle\nCreate a human-readable explanation of the success criteria. Do not output raw objects, JSON, arrays, trigger groups, or condition structures.\n\nInstead:\n\n1 Explain what a participant must do to be considered successful.\n2 Make sure to explain the participant action using behaviorDisplayName, conditions, attribute name, operator and value.\n3 Consider and share the exact condition values of each field from objects.\n4 Inside conditions object attribute name and values are linked, for example if attribute name is \"AutomationName\" and value has \"TPL-CS-SEG-EMAIL-001\" then , in combine its AutomationName is TPL-CS-SEG-EMAIL-001.\n5 Keep the response under 100 words.\n\nExample\nA participant is considered successful when they click through from the email ‘ERP Excellence: FDI Customer Success Stories from Your Industry’ to the ‘LP-12345’ landing page and submits the ‘Demo Request’ form on that page.\n\n\nSummary: \n\nUse expectedResult to explain the target in percentage format.\n\n1 Convert decimal values to percentages (e.g., 0.03 → 3%, 0.15 → 15%).\n2 Do not display raw decimal values.\n3 Keep the response under 20 words.\n\nExample:\n“At least 3% of participants must meet this success criterion.”"
            }
          ],
